<header><h1>Frontier Tokens: Proof</h1></header>
<article>
<p>The source text behind each note on <a href="/R_frontier_tokens">Frontier Tokens</a>. <b>Explicit</b> sources state the note directly. <b>Implicit</b> sources support it without stating it.</p>

<h2>Notes</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Players may explore space areas that contain frontier tokens if they own the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Dark_Energy_Tap"><i>Dark Energy Tap</i></a> technology or if another game effect allows them to.<sup>1,8</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>1</sup> LRR 35.4: &ldquo;Players can explore space areas that contain frontier tokens if they own the &lsquo;Dark Energy Tap&rsquo; technology or if another game effect allows them to.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>8</sup> PoK rulebook p. 16: &ldquo;If an ability instructs a player to explore a frontier token, they may do so even if they do not have the &lsquo;Dark Energy Tap&rsquo; technology.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If a system tile contains a <a href="/R_space_stations">space station</a>, but no planets, then a frontier token will be placed in that system during game setup.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 16: &ldquo;A system that contains a space station and no planets gets a frontier token during setup.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>Frontier tokens are not placed in systems in <a href="/R_fracture">The Fracture</a> when it is brought into play, as frontier tokens are only placed during setup. However, if The Fracture is in play when the <a href="/F_empyrean">Empyrean</a> player resolves their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Empyrean#Leaders:~:text=Multiverse%20Shift"><i>Multiverse Shift</i></a> hero ability, frontier tokens will be placed in the systems in The Fracture that do not contain a planet.<sup>2,6</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>6</sup> Community consensus: &ldquo;Are frontier tokens placed in The Fracture when it enters play? What about when the Empyrean hero is purged? A: No, Frontier tokens are placed during setup and the fracture is not in play at this time. The Empyrean Hero will place frontier tokens into the empty systems of the Fracture if it is in play.&rdquo;</li>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>2</sup> RulesPal, &ldquo;Do empty Fracture systems get frontier tokens, and can wormholes go there?&rdquo;: &ldquo;Not at the start: frontier tokens are placed at setup, before the Fracture is in play, though the Empyrean hero can later put them on its empty systems.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    <li>If <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Thunder&#x27;s_Edge">Thunder&rsquo;s Edge</a> is placed in a system containing a frontier token, that token is not removed.<sup>7</sup>
        <ul>
        <li><b>Explicit</b>: <sup>7</sup> Thunder&rsquo;s Edge Rulebook p. 16: &ldquo;When Thunder&rsquo;s Edge is placed into a system that contains a frontier token, do not remove the frontier token; it can still be explored.&rdquo;</li>
        </ul></li>
    </ol>
</article>
